<h2 id="key-features">⚙️ Key Features for Multi-Location Operators</h2>

<h3>Sub-Account Architecture</h3>

This is the core of why GoHighLevel works for multi-location businesses. Each location operates in its own sub-account with:

- Separate contact databases (no cross-contamination)
- Location-specific pipelines and stages
- Individual phone numbers and email sending domains
- Dedicated reporting and analytics
- Custom automations that can be templated from the parent account

You build a workflow once, snapshot it, and deploy across all locations. When you improve that workflow, push updates selectively or globally. This templating capability saved our team approximately 200 hours during initial setup.

<h3>Unified Inbox</h3>

Every location's communications — SMS, email, Facebook Messenger, Instagram DMs, Google Business Messages, web chat — flow into one inbox per location. Staff see a single conversation thread per customer regardless of channel.

For operators, this means visibility into response times and conversation quality across all locations from one dashboard. We identified two underperforming locations purely through inbox analytics — average response times were 4x higher than the group average.

<h3>Reputation Management</h3>

Automated review requests via SMS and email after customer interactions. Location-specific Google review links. Centralized monitoring of reviews across all locations with alerts for negative feedback.

Our restaurant group saw a 47% increase in Google review volume within 90 days of implementation. The automated follow-up sequences for customers who didn't leave a review on first request drove 31% of total new reviews.

<h3>Pipeline Management</h3>

Visual pipelines that track leads through your sales process. Each location can have identical pipeline structures (for easy comparison) or customized stages based on their specific services.

The pipeline reporting across locations revealed our fitness franchise had a 23% higher close rate at locations that followed up within 5 minutes versus 30+ minutes. We automated that insight into an immediate follow-up trigger.

<h3>Marketing Automation</h3>

Email and SMS campaigns with conditional logic, wait steps, and webhook integrations. You can build sequences like:

- New lead → immediate text → wait 5 min → if no response → email with video → wait 24 hours → second SMS
- Review left → tag customer → add to VIP sequence → birthday automation enrollment

The automation builder is drag-and-drop but powerful. We've built sequences with 30+ steps and multiple conditional branches without hitting limitations.

<h3>Appointment Scheduling</h3>

Built-in calendar system that replaces Calendly or Acuity. Round-robin assignment across team members, buffer times, integration with Google and Outlook calendars, and automated confirmation/reminder sequences.

<div class="callout-blue">
<strong>Pro Tip:</strong> Set up location-specific booking links with UTM parameters. GoHighLevel tracks the source, giving you actual ROI data on which marketing channels drive booked appointments, not just leads.
</div>

<h3>Funnel and Website Builder</h3>

Landing page builder with templates optimized for lead capture. Not as sophisticated as dedicated tools like Unbounce, but sufficient for most operator needs. Each location can have branded landing pages that feed into location-specific pipelines.

<h3>Missed-Call Text-Back</h3>

When a call goes unanswered, the system automatically texts the caller. Our restaurant group configured this to say: "Sorry we missed your call! Reply here to make a reservation or ask a question." This single feature recovered 340+ reservations monthly that would have otherwise gone to competitors.

